WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.810
"Festival"

00:00:02.810 --> 00:00:03.900
Finished!

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:06.490
Whoa... That's amazing, Bertholdt.

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:07.780
That's pretty good.

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:11.950
This is the one thing I'm good at.

00:01:47.110 --> 00:01:49.960
Period 9
Sweet Summer! Titan Junior High School

00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:51.840
Bertholdt...

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:53.760
Hey, Bertholdt!

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:55.430
How can he sleep like that?

00:01:55.640 --> 00:01:58.560
There he goes sleeping
in an artistic pose again.

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:01.140
I bet it'll be sunny tomorrow.

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:02.850
Wake up, Bertholdt!

00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:05.600
- Sorry.

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:07.230
- Ow, ow, ow...

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:08.940
Good morning, Reiner.

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:11.860
Bertholdt, I have an important favor to ask.

00:02:12.070 --> 00:02:12.990
What is it?

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:15.780
W-Well...

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:20.330
I'm thinking of asking Christa out
to the summer festival coming up soon.

00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:23.040
- Good luck.

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:24.040
- What?!

00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:25.540
You come with us, too!

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:28.540
Well, what's the point of me going with you?

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:31.960
Of course, I wanna go alone with her!

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:33.050
But...

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:34.380
But...?

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:36.590
I-I feel embarrassed.

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:40.560
Hey, is that all you have to say?

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:42.810
Smirk.

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:45.480
So, you invite someone, too.

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:47.850
I-Invite someone? Who?

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:49.730
For example, Annie.

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:51.940
Wh-Wh-Wh-What?!

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:54.150
- Th-Th-There isn't anyone I wanna ask!

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:55.650
- He's an open book.

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:59.660
Hey, Ymir. I wanna stop by
this crepe place on our way home.

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:00.740
You're gonna gain weight again.

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:01.990
What?!

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:04.620
Got a minute, Christa?

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:09.630
Would you like to go to the
summer festival with us this Saturday?

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:11.500
Would... you...?

00:03:11.710 --> 00:03:12.500
Sure, I'll go!

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:13.300
- Really?!

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:14.710
- H-Hey, wait!

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:17.340
You promised that you'd go
to the summer festival with me!

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:21.640
Yeah. It'll be more fun
if we all go together, right?!

00:03:21.850 --> 00:03:23.270
Who else shall we invite?

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:23.850
- I really think that the more the merrier when we go to a festival.

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:28.440
- Hey, Mr. Berthol, say some—

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:32.980
Oh, yeah! I wonder if they have a crepe stall...

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:34.860
I wanna eat some crepes, too.

00:03:35.070 --> 00:03:35.860
Smirk.

00:03:36.070 --> 00:03:38.610
Mr. Berthol, I have to stay
with Christa at the festival

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:41.780
so that my precious Christa
won't be attacked by a gorilla.

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:42.700
A gorilla?

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:45.120
So you invite someone, too.

00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:48.000
Someone like Annie.

00:03:48.210 --> 00:03:49.540
Wh-Wh-Wh-What?!

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:51.080
- Wh-Wh-Why would I ask Annie?!

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:52.960
- He is such an open book.

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:56.720
Hey, Annie! Bertholdt wants to talk to you.

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:58.590
Wha—?! Reiner?!

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:01.050
Are we doing it? Right here, right now?!

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:01.890
Yeah!

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:05.390
Now's the time! Do it!

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:06.890
What is it?

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:08.140
U-Uhm...

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:11.560
U-U-Uhm... Well...

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:15.110
Th-The summer festival coming up...!
Would you like to go with us?

00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:18.280
Summer festival? I'm not interested.

00:04:18.490 --> 00:04:20.410
Oh, summer festival, huh?

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:21.870
Sounds cool! I'll go! I'll go!

00:04:22.070 --> 00:04:23.740
If Eren goes, I'll go, too.

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:25.580
Sounds like fun. I'll go, too.

00:04:25.790 --> 00:04:27.290
<i>Yakisoba</i>! Cotton candy! Shaved ice!

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:29.000
Grilled squid! Octopus dumplings! Candy apples!

00:04:29.210 --> 00:04:30.920
I wonder if they have a fried chicken stall.

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:34.630
Humph! I'll teach you guys
how to enjoy festivals!

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:38.630
All right! Sounds like
it'll be fun! Right, Annie?

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:40.680
- What? I didn't...
- Okay, decided!

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:45.760
Th-They're coming, too?

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:49.390
A bunch of unwanted people are coming, too,

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:52.440
but at any rate, I'm glad that
you were able to invite Annie.

00:04:52.650 --> 00:04:54.400
Well, I wasn't really...

00:04:54.610 --> 00:04:58.440
Bertholdt... so you're still saying that stuff.

00:04:58.650 --> 00:05:00.780
Let's put an end to this.

00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:04.700
Tell Annie how you feel
about her at the festival.

00:05:04.910 --> 00:05:07.910
Huh? Wh-What're you...

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:11.960
You stare at her so much
that anyone, not just me, can tell.

00:05:12.170 --> 00:05:12.540
Wha—?!

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:15.920
It was so obvious that you were staring at her.

00:05:16.130 --> 00:05:17.630
Mr. Stare-thol.

00:05:20.010 --> 00:05:21.680
Calm down, Bertholdt.

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:25.640
In any case, this is a chance
for you to get closer to her.

00:05:25.850 --> 00:05:30.180
But aren't those guys a royal pain in the neck?

00:05:30.390 --> 00:05:32.190
It's true that it's a matter of life or death,

00:05:32.390 --> 00:05:34.980
but it's impossible to get rid of them now.

00:05:35.190 --> 00:05:39.320
You're right. This really is a crappy situation.

00:05:39.530 --> 00:05:41.860
But don't worry. I've got a plan.

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:43.860
- A plan? Better not be a stupid one.

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:45.910
- All I want is...

00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:49.950
...to be by Annie's side, that's all...

00:05:54.460 --> 00:05:57.630
Look. If you simply follow the plan,
you'll be fine, okay?

00:05:57.840 --> 00:05:59.340
O-Okay.

00:05:59.550 --> 00:06:03.720
Operation 1!
First, compliment her by saying she's cute!

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:08.350
Annie... You're very cute.
Such a pretty candy coating.

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:09.850
Bertholdt...

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:12.180
I love you.

00:06:12.980 --> 00:06:15.650
The key is to compliment her
about one specific thing.

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:16.560
Okay.

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:18.860
Thanks for waiting!

00:06:19.070 --> 00:06:22.780
Sorry! It took me a while to put this on.

00:06:22.990 --> 00:06:25.070
Sh-She's cute!

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:27.530
N-No, we didn't wait at all!

00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:30.450
Anyway, Christa, you look cute in that yuka—

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:32.750
You look cute wearing yukata, too, Christa!

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:35.790
Marry me once this festival is over.

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:37.290
Thanks.

00:06:38.630 --> 00:06:41.210
Now, Mr. Berthol, say something to Annie.

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:42.510
What? U-Uhm...

00:06:42.710 --> 00:06:44.170
Now. Say it!

00:06:46.550 --> 00:06:47.970
U-Uhm...

00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:52.220
Mr. Berthol, what were you
saying about Annie's yukata?

00:06:53.560 --> 00:06:56.480
Er... A-Annie...

00:06:56.690 --> 00:06:58.060
Now! Say it!

00:06:58.270 --> 00:07:00.730
That's a pretty knot on that geta strap.

00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:01.940
Ouch...

00:07:02.150 --> 00:07:04.070
Th-That's <i>too</i> specific.

00:07:04.280 --> 00:07:05.570
Hey!

00:07:05.780 --> 00:07:08.530
Is this where we're meeting up?!

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:10.950
You look very pretty in that yukata, Annie!

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:13.290
M-My dad got it for me.

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:17.000
Ymir. Reiner.
What're you doing down there?

00:07:17.210 --> 00:07:19.080
Now, where should we go first?

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:23.510
Eren, your mom said that you
should use your allowance carefully.

00:07:23.710 --> 00:07:26.470
I wanna eat some octopus dumplings.

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:28.340
You look cute in a yukata, too, Christa!

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:29.930
You aren't wearing a yukata, Sasha?

00:07:30.140 --> 00:07:32.310
- It feels tight around my belly when I wear a yukata, so I'm wearing a <i>jinbei</i>!

00:07:32.310 --> 00:07:33.260
- We'll move on to the next plan!

00:07:33.470 --> 00:07:37.770
Operation 2! Show her your manly side
by playing a shooting game!

00:07:37.980 --> 00:07:41.940
Shooting games are the best way
to show your manliness at a festival.

00:07:42.150 --> 00:07:44.360
H-Hey guys, would you like
to play a shooting game?

00:07:44.570 --> 00:07:45.570
Oh, sounds good!

00:07:45.780 --> 00:07:49.700
Hey kids! Welcome! I'm Ness.
I'm the owner of this stall.

00:07:49.910 --> 00:07:52.120
And, this is my pet hamster, Charrette.

00:07:52.330 --> 00:07:56.290
She likes to pull people's hair,
so be careful if you don't wanna become bald.

00:07:56.500 --> 00:07:57.370
Hey! Oops.

00:07:57.580 --> 00:07:58.370
- S-Stop it, Charrette! Hey! S-Someone, hold her down!

00:07:58.370 --> 00:08:01.500
- They say that a man who can shoot through the target in a shooting game

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:04.550
can shoot an arrow through
a woman's heart, too.

00:08:06.670 --> 00:08:08.510
Here, Annie.

00:08:08.720 --> 00:08:11.050
I won it for you.

00:08:11.260 --> 00:08:13.300
Bertholdt...

00:08:13.510 --> 00:08:14.760
I love you.

00:08:16.350 --> 00:08:17.680
Mikasa's amazing!

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:17.890
<b>Big Pork
Fillet Cutlet</b>

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:21.270
She got that huge one on her first try.

00:08:23.860 --> 00:08:25.900
Eren. This is for you.

00:08:26.110 --> 00:08:27.610
What's this all about?

00:08:27.820 --> 00:08:30.360
You looked like you wanted
the Big Pork Fillet Cutlet.

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:32.280
What kind of look is that?!

00:08:42.210 --> 00:08:44.790
Incredible! She did it on her first try, too!

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:49.840
Well, in short... does this mean
that we can have that?

00:08:50.050 --> 00:08:52.140
Mister! One more time!

00:08:57.390 --> 00:08:59.350
Please don't run me out of business.

00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:02.150
O-Okay, so maybe winning
something isn't the way to go.

00:09:02.350 --> 00:09:06.020
D-Don't worry! My plan still has a trump card!

00:09:06.230 --> 00:09:08.190
It'll completely turn things around!

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:11.240
I-It's hot, isn't it?
Would you like to have some shaved ice?

00:09:11.450 --> 00:09:12.610
Oh, that's a good idea!

00:09:12.820 --> 00:09:13.820
Would you like some, too, Annie?

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:15.030
Well, I—

00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:18.330
Shaved ice, huh?! Since I want
to have it right now, I'll go buy it!

00:09:18.540 --> 00:09:19.250
I'll go, too!

00:09:19.450 --> 00:09:21.210
Hey, wait you guys!

00:09:22.420 --> 00:09:25.380
Well, whatever.
We'll just put our plan into action.

00:09:25.590 --> 00:09:30.300
Operation 3! Operation "Watch out!
Your yukata's gonna get stained!"

00:09:30.510 --> 00:09:32.680
First, Ymir goes and buys shaved ice.

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:34.390
Oops!

00:09:34.590 --> 00:09:37.470
Just when the shaved ice
is about to get on Annie...

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:39.020
Splash!

00:09:41.940 --> 00:09:43.650
Are you okay, Annie?

00:09:43.850 --> 00:09:47.770
Bertholdt... Actually, a cold
chocolate-coated banana kinda looks good.

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:50.070
Ahh... I love you.

00:09:50.280 --> 00:09:52.400
You can turn things around with this!

00:09:52.610 --> 00:09:53.280
But...

00:09:53.490 --> 00:09:56.570
At any rate, I wonder
what's taking those two so long.

00:09:56.780 --> 00:10:00.200
...the wrong people went to buy the shaved ice.

00:10:00.410 --> 00:10:02.580
I bet they're lost.

00:10:02.790 --> 00:10:04.420
Thank you!

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:06.040
Annie?

00:10:11.260 --> 00:10:13.510
Dammit! As it stands, the operation isn't...

00:10:13.720 --> 00:10:16.220
What do we do? Should we change the plan?

00:10:16.430 --> 00:10:17.970
Reiner.

00:10:18.180 --> 00:10:19.390
Let's just forget about the plan.

00:10:19.600 --> 00:10:21.890
Huh? You're saying this now?

00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:23.600
We're trying to help you.

00:10:23.810 --> 00:10:27.770
It really isn't nice to put
Annie in danger for my sake.

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:29.440
We're finally out!

00:10:29.650 --> 00:10:32.690
Seriously, it was your fault
for trying to take a shortcut.

00:10:32.900 --> 00:10:34.240
What took you so long?

00:10:34.450 --> 00:10:36.320
Thanks for waiting. Here's the shaved ice.

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:38.450
What's this? It's melted.

00:10:38.660 --> 00:10:40.030
If you don't want it, I'll have it.

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:40.910
- Hey, stop it!

00:10:40.910 --> 00:10:42.790
- Smirk.

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:44.290
Oops!

00:10:44.500 --> 00:10:46.250
Annie! Watch out!

00:10:54.090 --> 00:10:55.170
Bertholdt...

00:10:55.380 --> 00:10:57.800
It didn't get on your yukata, did it?

00:10:58.010 --> 00:10:59.640
N-No...

00:10:59.850 --> 00:11:00.810
Good.

00:11:01.010 --> 00:11:03.890
W-Well, Annie!
Good thing that you were with Bertholdt!

00:11:04.100 --> 00:11:07.650
Y-Yeah! That was cool, Mr. Berthol.

00:11:07.850 --> 00:11:10.480
Bertholdt, are you okay?

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:13.570
I'll go wash my clothes.

00:11:13.780 --> 00:11:15.450
Sorry, I'll be back.

00:11:15.650 --> 00:11:17.320
Oh, hey.

00:11:32.210 --> 00:11:35.970
What was I thinking,
trying to do such a terrible thing to her?

00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:38.180
Come one, come all!

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:41.890
Come right up and enjoy
some super-fun die-cutting!

00:11:42.100 --> 00:11:42.720
Did you find him?

00:11:42.930 --> 00:11:44.560
He wasn't over there.

00:11:44.770 --> 00:11:46.930
I wonder where Bertholdt went...

00:11:47.140 --> 00:11:50.190
Dammit! We probably
got a little too carried away.

00:11:50.400 --> 00:11:53.190
Anyway, let's scatter and look for him.

00:11:55.690 --> 00:11:58.150
100 yen for 1 sheet

00:12:02.990 --> 00:12:03.950
Done.

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:07.000
Would you quit now?

00:12:07.210 --> 00:12:11.380
If you keep that pace up,
you're gonna drive me bankrupt.

00:12:11.580 --> 00:12:13.460
Here, prizes for you.

00:12:13.670 --> 00:12:14.750
Both of them?

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:18.470
One for you... and the
other for your girlfriend.

00:12:18.680 --> 00:12:22.140
Sh-She isn't my girlfriend!

00:12:23.810 --> 00:12:26.350
We're supposed to meet up here
once we find you,

00:12:26.560 --> 00:12:29.060
so I think the other guys will be here soon.

00:12:29.270 --> 00:12:33.230
I see... Sorry for causing you guys trouble.

00:12:33.440 --> 00:12:37.650
You've always liked die-cutting.

00:12:37.860 --> 00:12:39.320
You remembered?

00:12:39.530 --> 00:12:44.410
Yeah, so I had a hunch
that you'd be there today, too.

00:12:44.620 --> 00:12:46.540
I see.

00:12:46.740 --> 00:12:49.250
I haven't been to a summer festival
for a long time.

00:12:49.460 --> 00:12:52.080
Sorry for asking you to come along suddenly.

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:55.500
I hope you're having fun.

00:12:55.710 --> 00:12:59.760
I... don't like crowded places.

00:12:59.970 --> 00:13:00.880
I'm sorry!

00:13:01.090 --> 00:13:05.260
But... it might've been good
that you asked me to come along.

00:13:05.470 --> 00:13:06.470
What?

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:09.230
I'm not saying that I wanted to come with you,

00:13:09.430 --> 00:13:11.520
but I don't have to push myself
to make conversation,

00:13:11.730 --> 00:13:13.440
and I can be myself.

00:13:13.650 --> 00:13:15.900
I feel at ease with you.

00:13:16.110 --> 00:13:17.610
In other words...

00:13:17.820 --> 00:13:19.320
...you're pretty convenient to have around?

00:13:19.530 --> 00:13:22.110
Hey, that doesn't even sound like a friend!

00:13:22.320 --> 00:13:25.160
That's right. Something is a bit off.
Maybe you're like "air" to me?

00:13:25.370 --> 00:13:27.160
That's even worse!

00:13:32.170 --> 00:13:34.830
Ah! Hey! Bertho—

00:13:37.840 --> 00:13:39.260
Sorry.

00:13:42.340 --> 00:13:43.890
- But...
- Uhm...

00:13:47.050 --> 00:13:48.350
Annie...

00:13:48.560 --> 00:13:51.930
Uhm... Will you...

00:14:09.040 --> 00:14:10.200
Okay.

00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:11.540
All right!

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:16.330
Guys!

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:19.090
You did it, Bertholdt!

00:14:19.300 --> 00:14:22.670
I knew you could do it.

00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:23.880
Thanks.

00:14:24.090 --> 00:14:26.680
Well then, let's all do some die-cutting!

00:14:27.800 --> 00:14:29.760
100 yen for 1 sheet

00:14:33.600 --> 00:14:37.100
So she said okay to doing die-cutting together?

00:14:37.310 --> 00:14:39.690
That was the perfect moment
we'd been waiting for, and yet...

00:14:39.900 --> 00:14:41.360
Argh! It cracked again!

00:14:41.570 --> 00:14:43.860
You really are good at it, Bertholdt.

00:14:44.070 --> 00:14:46.990
The trick to die-cutting is patience.

00:14:47.200 --> 00:14:49.780
If you become hasty and
press it hard, it cracks easily.

00:14:49.990 --> 00:14:51.740
- So you have to stay calm and cut carefully, like you're scraping the gap.

00:14:51.740 --> 00:14:53.330
- Oh, well.

00:14:55.750 --> 00:14:57.790
Whoa! That's so cool!

00:14:58.000 --> 00:14:59.420
They're beautiful.

00:14:59.630 --> 00:15:01.500
<i>Tamaya</i>!

00:15:03.420 --> 00:15:04.760
How beautiful...

00:15:10.100 --> 00:15:11.930
<i>Tamaya</i>!

00:15:17.140 --> 00:15:22.400
<i>The time to fight back has come,</i>
<i>climb over that wall</i>

00:15:22.610 --> 00:15:28.160
<i>Like a lighthouse, ignite the light of hope</i>

00:15:28.360 --> 00:15:33.660
<i>That enormous strength is precisely</i>
<i>what leads the way to freedom</i>

00:15:33.870 --> 00:15:39.380
<i>Let's look beyond this conflict, Ausfall!</i>

00:15:49.050 --> 00:15:54.470
<i>Inside the wall, with no place to run,</i>

00:15:54.680 --> 00:16:00.150
<i>we're stuck in restrictions and exploits</i>

00:16:00.350 --> 00:16:04.690
<i>Even if our glory days of youth</i>
<i>get trampled upon,</i>

00:16:04.900 --> 00:16:10.320
<i>I want to at least hold on to the future</i>

00:16:10.530 --> 00:16:16.200
<i>I won't give in to that</i>
<i>absurd scolding voice, either</i>

00:16:16.410 --> 00:16:21.920
<i>I pledged to the earth that I'd make</i>
<i>our dreams and hopes come true</i>

00:16:22.130 --> 00:16:27.300
<i>The time to fight back has come,</i>
<i>the blood in my veins calls forth the future</i>

00:16:27.510 --> 00:16:33.100
<i>We'll pull apart all those troublesome rules</i>

00:16:33.300 --> 00:16:38.560
<i>Now's the time to raise the flag</i>
<i>of revolt upon that steep wall</i>

00:16:38.770 --> 00:16:44.190
<i>Seek prosperity, Ausfall!</i>

00:16:45.520 --> 00:16:48.110
The student council president election...

00:16:48.320 --> 00:16:51.110
Many students run in order
to pursue their own ambitions.

00:16:51.110 --> 00:16:52.870
<b>Rico</b>

00:16:52.870 --> 00:16:53.160
Many students run in order
to pursue their own ambitions.

00:16:53.370 --> 00:16:56.990
